## Question 1a

> What is the average score for kids in the treatment group in period 1 of the study? What is the average score for the same kids in period 2?

The treatment group averaged -0.72 in period one, or the constant, and 2.19 in period 2. (-0.72+2.91 = 2.19).


## Question 1b

> Explain what it means when b0 is statistically significant in the reflexive model. Explain what it means when b1 is statistically significant.

When b0 is significant, the treatment group's average ability score in T1 is statistically different from zero. A significant b1 means the change, or gain, in ability from T1 to T2 is statistically different from zero. An example would be tjhat the group's average score moved significantly between the two time periods. 


## Question 1c

> What is the effect size according to this model?

The effect size in the relexive model is b1=2.91. Which is the raw pre-post gain for the treatment group. 


