           intercept.top=TRUE, intercept.bottom=FALSE,
           digits=2 )
```

## Question 7

> Which coefficient captures the parallel lines test? Do we want it to be significant or not?

The interaction or treat.post coefficient captures the parallel lines test, testing whether the pre-treatment trend differs between groups. This coefficient needs to not be statistically significant, a non-significant interaction supports the parallel treat assumption, where the two groups were moving similarly prior to treatment initiation. Both pre-tests here support this, with the high-SES treat.post=-0.43 and is non-significant, and control treat.post =-0.08 which is also non-significant and passes the parallel-trends check.  

























